<div class="policies">
    <p class="bold center" style="margin: 22px 0 8px;">HUMAN RESOURCE POLICIES</p>
    <p>The following policies are applicable to all employees of the organization. Employees are required to read, understand, and adhere to these policies at all times.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">1. Salary Structure and Payment</p>
    <p>The salary cycle is from 1st to 30th/31st of each month. Salary will be credited between the 10th and 13th of the following month. Salary will only be disbursed after the completion of one full working month. Salary details are confidential and must not be disclosed.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">2. Attendance, Leave &amp; Working Hours Policy</p>
    <p>Employees are entitled to 4 weekly offs per month. Any additional leave (other than weekly offs) will be treated as Leave Without Pay (LWP) unless prior approval is obtained.</p>
    <p>Late arrival up to 5 minutes will be marked as Late (LC). 3 instances of LC = ½ Day Leave deduction. Arrival beyond 5 minutes = ½ Day deduction. Uninformed absence will be treated as Absent (A). 1 day uninformed absence = deduction of 2 days’ salary.</p>
    <p>Employees must achieve their assigned Login Time / Call Time / Talk Time targets, failing which the day will be marked as Half Day/Absent.</p>
    <p>Medical leave will only be considered upon submission of valid medical documents.</p>
    <p>All employees must successfully clear training certification/mock assessments, failing which salary may not be paid or employment may be terminated.</p>
    <p>Biometric scanning is compulsory for all the employees as attendance will be calculated on the basis of biometric logs.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">3. Absconding Policy</p>
    <p>Continuous absence for 3 working days without approval will be treated as Absconding/Attrition (ATTR). In such cases, the employee will not be eligible for salary payout or relieving documentation.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">4. Probation Period</p>
    <p>All employees will serve a probation period of 6 months. Confirmation of employment will be based on performance, behavior, and attendance. The company reserves the right to extend the probation period if necessary.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">5. Process Allocation Policy</p>
    <p>Employees may be transferred or allocated to any process as per business requirements, irrespective of their initial process assignment.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">6. Salary Hold &amp; Split Release</p>
    <p>If an employee takes more than 2 Leaves/HDs/Unapproved WOs between the 1st–10th of the month, salary will be released in two parts: 50% on the 10th and the remaining 50% on the 20th, subject to continuation of employment.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">7. Exit &amp; Notice Period Policy</p>
    <p>Resignation is not permitted within the first 3 months of employment. A minimum 30-day’s written notice period is mandatory for L1 &amp; for L2 60 days’ notice period is mandatory Resignation will only be accepted if submitted between 25th–31st of any month and will be applicable from the 1st of the following month. Failure to serve notice or absconding will result in salary being withheld and the employee being marked as absconded.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">8. Personal Belongings Policy</p>
    <p>The company is not responsible for the safety of personal belongings such as mobile phones, headphones, jewelry, or cash.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">9. Mobile Usage Policy</p>
    <p>Use of mobile phones on the work floor is strictly prohibited. Violation will result in a ₹500 penalty deducted from salary.</p>

    <p class="policy-title">10. Zero Tolerance Policy (ZTP) &amp; Integrity Standards</p>
    <p>Any violation of integrity (misconduct, dishonesty, negligence) will result in a warning letter (communicated on employee’s official/personal email). 2 warning letters → On the 3rd violation, the employee will be asked to resign without salary or incentives</p>
    <p>Any fraud, fake work, or malpractice that causes financial or reputational loss to the company will lead to immediate termination without salary. Instances of harassment, misbehavior, or misconduct (verbal/physical, with colleagues of any gender/seniority) will lead to termination, legal/police action, and recovery of damages/financial loss or penalty charges will be recover from the employee.</p>
</div>
